We built \textbf{DisPeD} (Discourse-level Persuasion Detection), a two-stage framework with seven controlled Stage~1 variants that systematically decompose the mechanism: 9-class persuasion strategy classification, binary classification, scrambled labels, MLM only, topic classification, Wikipedia MLM, and vanilla control (Section~\ref{sec:method}). Each variant isolates a specific factor (domain exposure, classification supervision, label quality, label granularity, or domain specificity) while holding all other components constant, enabling causal attribution of detection performance to individual factors.

The result \emph{partially falsified} our original hypothesis that persuasion-specific classification is the key ingredient. MLM without labels achieves near-perfect early detection on unseen Deceptive Delight (mean F1\,$\geq$\,0.97 at $K \leq 5$), but shows instability at full conversation length (F1\,=\,0.91$\pm$0.12) while the 9-class model maintains 0.997$\pm$0.005. The evidence hierarchy is:

\vspace{2pt}
\noindent\hspace{0.5em}{\small vanilla (0.28) $<$ topic (0.54$\pm$0.21) $\ll$ wiki-MLM (0.90$\pm$0.12) $\approx$ jb-MLM (0.91$\pm$0.12) $<$ scrambled (0.99) $\approx$ binary (0.99) $\approx$ 9-class (0.997$\pm$0.005)}
\vspace{2pt}

\noindent Any continued pretraining bridges the dominant $\sim$62\,pp gap from vanilla. Wikipedia MLM nearly matches jailbreak-domain MLM at full length; the domain advantage is meaningful at early prefixes ($K$=2: 0.993 vs.\ 0.911) and for perturbation robustness. Only the 9-class model achieves F1\,=\,0.997$\pm$0.005 with near-zero variance. This connects to domain-adaptive pretraining~\citep{gururangan2020dontstop}: continued training captures pragmatic features, with classification supervision providing stability that unsupervised pretraining alone does not guarantee.

Our contributions:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*, itemsep=2pt, topsep=4pt]
  \item \textbf{Systematic decomposition of cross-attack generalization.} Seven controlled variants establish that continued pretraining bridges $\sim$62\,pp of the OOD gap; jailbreak-domain text improves early detection ($K$=2: 8\,pp over Wikipedia MLM). Misaligned supervision (topic F1\,=\,0.54$\pm$0.21) destabilizes generalization.

  \item \textbf{Classification supervision adds stability, robustness, and interpretability.} Classification-supervised variants achieve F1\,$\geq$\,0.99 with near-zero variance vs.\ MLM 0.91$\pm$0.12. Under perturbation ($n$=76), all classification-supervised variants (including scrambled labels) show zero degradation at full length vs.\ $\sim$12\,pp for non-adapted models. A three-layer robustness attribution emerges: classification structure provides full-length robustness, the combination of correct and fine-grained labels is required at $K$=2 (scrambled = binary = $-$2.6\,pp, neither alone suffices), and both properties contribute independently at $K$=1 (9-class $-$2.6\,pp vs.\ scrambled $-$5.3\,pp vs.\ binary $-$9.2\,pp). The persuasion taxonomy additionally provides distinct strategy trajectories per attack type (Section~\ref{sec:strategy}).
\end{itemize}

